---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LinkedText from '../components/LinkedText.astro';

// Constants from reference/XML/Infos/globalsInt.xml and culture.xml; mechanic
// transcribed from City.cs (getCaptureThreshold / setCaptureTurns / doTribeTurn).
//
//   CITY_BASE_CAPTURE_TURNS      = 2
//   CITY_CAPTURE_DAMAGE_PERCENT  = 50   (HP the city is left at after it flips)
//   culture.iExtraCaptureTurns:  Weak 0 · Developing 1 · Strong 2 · Legendary 3
//   +1 to the threshold when the capturer is NOT the city's original founder.

const BASE_TURNS = 2;

const cultures = [
  { name: 'Weak',       extra: 0 },
  { name: 'Developing', extra: 1 },
  { name: 'Strong',     extra: 2 },
  { name: 'Legendary',  extra: 3 },
];

// threshold = max(1, base + cultureExtra + (notFounder ? 1 : 0))
const rows = cultures.map(c => ({
  culture: c.name,
  extra: c.extra,
  foreign: Math.max(1, BASE_TURNS + c.extra + 1), // taking a city you didn't found
  own:     Math.max(1, BASE_TURNS + c.extra),     // retaking a city your team founded
}));
---

<Base
  title="City Capture Mechanics"
  active="city-capture-mechanics"
  pageMark="🏰"
  description="How long a city takes to flip after you occupy it in Old World: the capture-turns counter, the exact threshold formula (base + enemy culture level + the original-founder bonus), and the per-turn accrual rules — transcribed from City.cs."
  pageStats={[
    { label: 'base turns', value: BASE_TURNS },
    { label: 'capture HP left', value: '50%' },
  ]}
>
  <p class="lede">
    Taking a city is not instant. When your unit occupies an enemy city, a
    hidden <b>capture-turns counter</b> ticks up each turn you hold it; the city
    flips to you only when the counter reaches its <b>threshold</b>. Leave or
    get pushed off before then and the progress unwinds. The threshold depends
    on the city's <b>culture level</b> and on whether you originally founded it.
  </p>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">How the counter works</h2>
    <ul class="cc-bullets">
      <li>
        Each turn your unit is actively occupying the city
        (<code>isUnitCapturingCity</code>), the counter increases by
        <b>+1</b> (<code>changeCaptureTurns(1)</code>).
      </li>
      <li>
        The city flips the moment the counter reaches
        <code>getCaptureThreshold()</code> — control transfers and the city is
        left <b>damaged to 50% HP</b> (<code>CITY_CAPTURE_DAMAGE_PERCENT</code>).
      </li>
      <li>
        If no one is occupying it, the counter ticks <b>−1</b> per turn and
        resets to 0 — an interrupted capture is undone. You must hold the city
        <b>continuously</b> for the full count.
      </li>
      <li>
        Recapture / liberation also resets the counter to 0 when ownership
        changes (<code>setCaptureTurns(0)</code>).
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">The threshold formula</h2>
    <div class="cc-formula">
      <div class="cc-line">
        <span class="cc-eq">turns = CITY_BASE_CAPTURE_TURNS&nbsp;(2)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-line">
        <span class="cc-eq cc-add">+ culture(highest&nbsp;enemy&nbsp;culture).iExtraCaptureTurns</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-line">
        <span class="cc-eq cc-add">+ 1&nbsp;&nbsp;if you are NOT the city's original founder</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-line cc-min">
        <span class="cc-eq">→ minimum 1</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      The culture term uses the <b>highest culture level of any team other than
      the capturer</b> that has culture in the city — effectively the defender's
      cultural entrenchment. Per <code>culture.xml</code>
      (<code>iExtraCaptureTurns</code>):
    </p>

    <table class="cc-table cc-table--narrow">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>City culture</th><th class="cc-num">Extra turns</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {cultures.map(c => (
          <tr>
            <td><LinkedText text={c.name} /></td>
            <td class="cc-num"><b>+{c.extra}</b></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="cc-fineprint">
      The <b>+1 original-founder</b> term is <code>getCaptureTeam() !=
      getFirstTeam()</code>: it applies when you take a city your team did
      <b>not</b> found, so <b>retaking your own former city is exactly one turn
      faster</b> — and "your own" means the team that originally founded it, even
      if an enemy captured and grew it since.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">Turns to flip</h2>
    <p>
      Hold-time required, by the city's culture level and whether you founded it:
    </p>
    <table class="cc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>City culture</th>
          <th class="cc-num">Taking a foreign city</th>
          <th class="cc-num">Retaking your own</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map(r => (
          <tr>
            <td><LinkedText text={r.culture} /> <span class="cc-dim">(+{r.extra})</span></td>
            <td class="cc-num"><b>{r.foreign}</b></td>
            <td class="cc-num"><b>{r.own}</b></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="cc-fineprint">
      So a freshly-founded enemy outpost flips in <b>3</b> turns of unbroken
      occupation; an old <LinkedText text="Legendary" /> enemy capital takes
      <b>6</b>. Liberating one of your own cities shaves a turn off each.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">When a captured city is razed instead</h2>
    <p>
      On reaching the threshold, the city is normally transferred. It is
      <b>razed</b> instead in two cases (<code>setCaptureTurns</code>):
    </p>
    <ul class="cc-bullets">
      <li>
        A <LinkedText text="Tribe" /> captures it and the
        <code>GAMEOPTION_ALLOW_CITY_RAZING</code> option is on.
      </li>
      <li>
        A player captures it but is already at their <b>city cap</b>
        (<code>isCityMaxReached()</code>) — they can't hold another, so it burns.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">Worked example</h2>
    <ol class="cc-steps">
      <li>
        You assault a rival's <LinkedText text="Strong" />-culture city (you did
        not found it). Threshold = 2 (base) + 2 (Strong) + 1 (not founder) =
        <b>5</b>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your unit occupies the city. Each end of turn it holds, the counter goes
        1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5.
      </li>
      <li>
        If a relief force evicts your unit on, say, turn 3 (counter at 3), the
        counter starts falling −1/turn back toward 0 — you'd have to start over.
      </li>
      <li>
        Hold all 5 turns and the city flips to you at <b>50% HP</b>. If that same
        city had originally been <i>yours</i>, it would have flipped in
        <b>4</b>.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <p class="cc-source">
    Source: <code>City.cs</code> — <code>getCaptureThreshold()</code> (formula),
    <code>setCaptureTurns()</code> (flip / raze / 50% damage), and the
    <code>+1 / −1</code> accrual in <code>doTribeTurn()</code>. Constants from
    <code>globalsInt.xml</code> (<code>CITY_BASE_CAPTURE_TURNS</code>,
    <code>CITY_CAPTURE_DAMAGE_PERCENT</code>) and
    <code>culture.xml</code> (<code>iExtraCaptureTurns</code>).
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .lede b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-section { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .cc-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .cc-section p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin: 0.3rem 0;
  }
  .cc-section p b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-bullets {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    max-width: 80ch;
  }
  .cc-bullets li { padding: 0.2rem 0; }
  .cc-bullets b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-formula {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0.9rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .cc-line { padding: 0.12rem 0; }
  .cc-eq {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .cc-add { color: var(--text-dim); }
  .cc-min .cc-eq { color: var(--accent); }

  .cc-table {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 64ch;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 0.6rem 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .cc-table--narrow { max-width: 36ch; }
  .cc-table thead th {
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }
  .cc-table tbody td {
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .cc-table tbody tr:hover { background: var(--bg-elev); }
  .cc-num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .cc-num b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .cc-dim { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: 0.8em; }

  .cc-steps {
    list-style: decimal inside;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 72ch;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .cc-steps li { padding: 0.25rem 0; }
  .cc-steps b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-fineprint {
    color: var(--text-faint) !important;
    font-size: 0.78rem !important;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-style: italic;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .cc-fineprint b { color: var(--text-dim); }

  .cc-source {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 80ch;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78em;
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    padding: 0 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
